This works even if the Exchange Remote Mailbox cmdlets aren't available, and it shows the key values that SailPoint provisioning typically sets during remote mailbox creation.

Get-ADUser jsmith -Properties mail,mailNickname,targetAddress,msExchRemoteRecipientType |
    Select-Object `
        SamAccountName,
        @{Name="RemoteMailboxEnabled";Expression={$_.msExchRemoteRecipientType -ne $null}},
        @{Name="Alias";Expression={$_.mailNickname}},
        @{Name="PrimarySMTP";Expression={$_.mail}},
        @{Name="RemoteRoutingAddress";Expression={$_.targetAddress}},
        msExchRemoteRecipientType


